/P 548 0 R
/E (We are living in a time when humanity continues to experience the immeasurable love and unfailing goodness of God in countless ways. Yet, even after receiving such grace, many struggle to honor God wholeheartedly, to live selflessly, to forgive one another, and to uphold the dignity and worth of fellow human beings. In the midst of such spiritual realities, the Church is called to proclaim once again the transforming message of the Gospel that renews hearts, restores relationships, and leads people into the fullness of life in Christ.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 548 0 R
/E (As we enter the month of June, the themes placed before us by the Church are deeply relevant not only to our personal spiritual journeys but also to the challenges faced by Christian communities in the United States today. These reflections invite us to examine whether our faith is merely a tradition we practice or a living witness that shapes our thoughts, relationships, decisions, and daily conduct.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
